    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "A number, $x$, is doubled and the result is divided by 8. Write this using algebraic notation. If $x = 7$, what is the final result?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\frac{x}{4}$; when $x=7$, $1\\frac{3}{4}$.",
      "worked": "The expression is $\\frac{2x}{8}=\\frac{x}{4}$.\n\nFor $x=7$:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{x}{4}&=\\frac{7}{4}\\\\\\frac{x}{4}&=1\\frac{3}{4}\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
